cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "cti-suite: eight packages for one intelligence cycle"
abstract: >-
  A workspace of eight packages that run one CTI cycle: requirements, alias
  reconciliation, a graded ledger, a hunt plan, a STIX product and a pre-share gate.
  Every tool refuses something the cycle should not allow; the grade a claim may carry is
  capped by the evidence behind it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Eliseo"
    given-names: "Martín"
    alias: "Falsifyer"
    website: "https://falsifyer.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Falsifyer/Defensible-CTI"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cyber threat intelligence
  - threat intelligence lifecycle
  - STIX 2.1
  - TLP 2.0
  - analysis of competing hypotheses
  - threat hunting
version: "0.1.0"  # the cti-suite facade; the workspace has no single version
date-released: "2026-10-22"
notes: >-
  Current package versions: cti-method 0.2.0, cryptonym 0.7.0, assessment-mcp 0.3.0,
  sharegate 0.2.0, stix-forge 0.2.0, pir-ledger 0.2.0, huntplan 0.2.0, cti-suite 0.1.0.
